' F11 -- LLM provider failover (text chains).
' Chapter 4. UML activity diagram.
' Pinned revision dfc20df6 (2026-11-06). Claim supported: the chains hold eight
' entries on six credentials; failures are classified five ways (402, 429,
' 401, 404, other) and only the last class carries no penalty. A 401 (key
' rejected) disables like 402 and 404; a 403 stays "other" on purpose, since
' OpenRouter answers a moderation-flagged prompt with 403.
' Sources: backend/services/ai/orchestrator.py (registry :239-367, chains
' :386-397, availability :672-742, rotation :1019-1169 with
' 401 at :1126-1135 + :1148-1155, wrappers :1512-1617),
' backend/services/llm_client.py:34-79, backend/services/ai/vision.py:117-209
' (401/402/404 permanent :177-195).
@startuml f11-provider-chain
!include _style.iuml

title LLM failover: 8 chain entries, 6 credentials

start
:pick BULK or QUALITY chain;
if (user's monthly budget left?) then (no: LLMBudgetExceededError)
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:refresh fleet counters, preferred first,
then filter the chain, in order
hard: disabled · no key · OpenAI ceiling
soft: daily limit · backoff window
(soft gates relaxed if nothing passes,
never a fallback to the raw chain);
note right
  Still weak:
  gemma+gemini, groq_fast+groq share keys
  8 attempts budgeted, at most 4 fit in 25 s
end note
while (next provider?) is (yes)
  if (outcome?) then (ok)
    :count, cost,\nreturn; <<#BFBFBF>>
    stop
  elseif (402) then (yes)
    :disable until\nrestart (billing);
  elseif (429 (text)) then (yes)
    :backoff 90 s·2^n,\nmax 600 s;
  elseif (401/404) then (yes)
    :disable until\nrestart (key\nor model);
  else (other)
    :no penalty,\n403 included; <<#DCDCDC>>
  endif
endwhile (none left: raise last error)
stop

legend bottom
  BULK      groq_fast > cloudflare > gemma > mistral > openrouter > gemini > groq > openai
  QUALITY  groq > openrouter > cloudflare > gemini > mistral > groq_fast > gemma > openai
  openai_only mode: both chains are [openai]. Vision: gemini > openai; 401/402/404 disable.
endlegend

@enduml
